<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal Jan-Dec global trade def 1,587.9 bln esc.</title>
<headline>Portugal Jan-Dec global trade def 1,587.9 bln esc.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's global trade deficit rose 4.0 percent to 1,587.9 billion escudos between January and December 1996 from 1,526.9 billion in the same period of 1995, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said.  </p>
<p>		   Jan-Dec 96 Jan-Dec 95  Dec '96    Dec '95</p>
<p> Overall balance  -1,587.9 -1,526.9   -169.1    -135.5</p>
<p> Imports	     5,265.4  5,028.7    425.4     412.5</p>
<p> Exports	     3,677.5  3,501.8    256.3     277.0</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in billions of escudos. A minus sign denotes a deficit. 1995 figures are definitive while 1996 figures are preliminary.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
